L3_SYSTEM = 'You are an accountant doing a careful VISUAL review of a Thai tax invoice. Another OCR + LLM chain has already extracted fields, but the result was FLAGGED for visual review (see trigger reasons below).\n\nYour task:\n1. Look at the IMAGE carefully — especially areas mentioned in the trigger reasons.\n2. Compare the image to (a) the OCR text from a previous engine and (b) the previous JSON extraction.\n3. CORRECT any wrong fields, FILL IN any missing fields you can read clearly from the IMAGE.\n4. Output the COMPLETE corrected ThaiInvoice JSON (not just diffs — full schema).\n5. When the IMAGE and the previous extraction DISAGREE, trust the IMAGE.\n6. When the IMAGE is unclear, fall back to the OCR text. When both are unclear, keep the previous value rather than guess.\n\nOutput ONE JSON object matching this schema (no markdown, no explanation, just JSON):\n\n{\n  "document_type": "tax_invoice" | "simplified_tax_invoice" | "receipt" | "credit_note" | "payment_evidence" | "order_evidence" | "other",\n  "is_not_invoice": false,\n  "is_copy_or_duplicate": false,\n  "invoice_number": "string or null",\n  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD Gregorian or null",\n  "date_raw": "exact date text as printed",\n  "seller_name": "string",\n  "seller_tax": "13-digit Thai tax ID or empty string",\n  "seller_branch": "5-digit branch or empty string",\n  "seller_addr": "string",\n  "buyer_name": "string",\n  "buyer_tax": "13-digit Thai tax ID or empty string",\n  "buyer_branch": "5-digit branch or empty string",\n  "buyer_addr": "string",\n  "subtotal": "number-as-string",\n  "vat": "number-as-string",\n  "wht_rate": "number-as-string",\n  "wht_amount": "number-as-string",\n  "discount": "total discount as printed (ส่วนลด), number-as-string, empty if none",\n  "total_amount": "FINAL net payable (Total/NET/ยอดสุทธิ), number-as-string or null",\n  "cash_amount": "cash tendered (เงินสด/รับเงิน/CASH), empty if not printed",\n  "change_amount": "change returned (เงินทอน/ทอน), empty if none",\n  "items": [{"name": "...", "qty": "...", "price": "...", "subtotal": "..."}],\n  "notes": "remark text",\n  "category": "3-5 char summary in items\' language",\n  "additional_invoices": [],\n  "source_refs": {\n    "invoice_number": {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "Invoice No."} or omit,\n    "total_amount":   {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "Total"     } or omit,\n    "subtotal":       {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "Subtotal"  } or omit,\n    "vat":            {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "VAT"       } or omit,\n    "seller_tax":     {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "Tax ID"    } or omit,\n    "buyer_tax":      {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "Tax ID"    } or omit,\n    "date":           {"value": "...", "source_text": "as printed", "source_column": "Date"      } or omit\n  }\n}\n\nPROVENANCE — fill source_refs for amount + tax-id + date fields with the exact printed column\nlabel of the cell the value came from. Validators reject amounts from Description/Remark/Address.\n\nCRITICAL RULES (same as previous extraction; pay attention):\n1. DATE: Buddhist year (>= 2400) MUST be converted to Gregorian by subtracting 543. e.g. 2569 -> 2026. ALWAYS fill date_raw with the original text.\n2. NAMES & ADDRESSES: Copy EXACTLY as printed (Thai or English). Do NOT auto-correct or standardize.\n3. ITEMS: read EVERY line item top to bottom, miss none. Thermal/POS receipts wrap one item over\n   2-3 lines (name, then qty x unit-price, then line total) — stitch into ONE item (name, qty,\n   price, subtotal). A row is an item only if it has a product/service name; SKIP subtotal / VAT /\n   total / change / cash / discount / table-no / thank-you rows. Self-check: item subtotals should\n   build toward the document subtotal. Keep ONE copy if the same name+qty+price is duplicated.\n4. NUMBERS: No currency symbols, no commas (e.g., "12450.00").\n5. TAX IDs: Exactly 13 digits, no dashes/spaces. Empty string if not found.\n5b. BRANCH (สาขา): seller_branch / buyer_branch = that party\'s branch as printed next to its name or tax ID, as 5 digits: "สำนักงานใหญ่" / "Head Office" / "HQ" -> "00000"; "สาขาที่ 18" / "สาขา 00018" / "Branch 18" -> "00018". Empty string when not printed. Never copy one party\'s branch to the other.\n6. WHT: Common rates 1/2/3/5%. wht_rate is the number ONLY ("3" not "3%").\n7. AMOUNT ARITHMETIC: When trigger reasons mention amount mismatch, look carefully at subtotal/vat/total in the image. The correct relationship is: subtotal + vat = total_amount (within rounding tolerance). Copy a printed VAT exactly; never recompute it from the total (VAT-exempt items make it smaller).\n7b. TOTAL vs PAYMENT: total_amount = FINAL net payable (Total/NET/ยอดสุทธิ), AFTER discount, NEVER\n   the cash tendered or change. Cash (เงินสด/รับเงิน)→cash_amount, change (เงินทอน/ทอน)→change_amount,\n   discount (ส่วนลด)→discount. "ยอดสุทธิ 110 / เงินสด 200 / เงินทอน 90" → total_amount=110 (NOT 200).\n8. is_not_invoice: true ONLY if clearly not an invoice. A FUEL/PETROL receipt (Bangchak/PTT/Shell · น้ำมัน/ดีเซล/liters+total) IS a receipt (TID/BATCH/TRACE = POS footer); is_not_invoice only for a bare card slip with no goods & no seller tax id.\n9. is_copy_or_duplicate: true if the text contains สำเนา / COPY / DUPLICATE markers.\n9b. INVOICE NUMBER on shop slips: "R#0000970791P2 :0302013" → invoice_number is the R# part; the ":0302013" after it is the store / POS code, never the invoice number.\n10. MULTIPLE INVOICES ON ONE PAGE (CRITICAL — a trigger may say a stacked invoice was\n    missed): one page can hold TWO+ separate tax invoices stacked vertically, each with its\n    OWN invoice number, buyer, total. Scan the WHOLE image top-to-bottom; put the topmost in\n    top-level fields and EACH remaining one as a COMPLETE object in "additional_invoices".\n    Every distinct invoice number appears exactly once — never merge or drop. Nested\n    additional_invoices stay []; one invoice → leave it [].\n'

_INDEPENDENT_REREAD = 'INDEPENDENT RE-READ (this overrides any habit of copying):\nThe OCR TEXT and PREVIOUS JSON show what an EARLIER pass produced. They are evidence of\nwhat may be WRONG, never a source of truth. For EVERY field you output, read the characters\noff the IMAGE yourself. Where the image and the OCR TEXT disagree, the IMAGE WINS.\nSingle-stroke digit confusions (5/6, 3/8, 0/9, 1/7) are the most common OCR failure and they\ndo NOT look wrong in the text — the Buddhist-era year is the highest-risk field: read its four\ndigits one by one off the image before writing date_raw.'

def build_l3_user_prompt(layer1_text, layer2_invoice, trigger_reasons):
    """Assemble the user-message text block (image is sent separately)."""
    if len(layer1_text) > MAX_TEXT_LENGTH:
        layer1_text = layer1_text[:MAX_TEXT_LENGTH] + '\n[...truncated]'
    triggers_block = '\n'.join((f'  - {t}' for t in trigger_reasons)) if trigger_reasons else '  - (no specific trigger; general visual review)'
    prev_json = layer2_invoice.model_dump(mode='json')
    prev_json_str = json.dumps(prev_json, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)
    return f'TRIGGER REASONS (why we are asking for visual review):\n{triggers_block}\n\nOCR TEXT (from Vision API, may have minor character errors):\n=== OCR TEXT ===\n{layer1_text}\n=== END OCR TEXT ===\n\nPREVIOUS EXTRACTION (may have errors flagged above):\n=== PREVIOUS JSON ===\n{prev_json_str}\n=== END PREVIOUS JSON ===\n\n{_INDEPENDENT_REREAD}\n\nNow look at the IMAGE and output the CORRECTED JSON only.'

L3_RETRY_HINT = '\n\nIMPORTANT — your previous response was invalid JSON. Common failure modes:\n  1. Unterminated string (missing closing double-quote)\n  2. Unescaped newline inside a string value\n  3. Missing comma between fields\n  4. Trailing comma after last field\nOutput exactly ONE complete JSON object. Close every string with a double-quote. Replace any literal newlines inside string values with spaces. Do NOT use markdown code fences. Do NOT add commentary before or after the JSON.'

RESCUE_SYSTEM = 'You are re-reading ONLY the totals/summary block of a Thai tax invoice or receipt image. A previous extraction of this block failed a consistency check (subtotal + vat != total, or vat is not ~7% of the taxable base) — at least one digit in this block was very likely misread.\n\nLook ONLY at the summary area (usually bottom-right or bottom of the document — labels like มูลค่าสินค้า/ก่อนภาษี, ภาษีมูลค่าเพิ่ม/VAT, ส่วนลด/Discount, รวมเป็นเงินทั้งสิ้น/Grand Total/Total). Read every digit carefully, digit by digit — Thailand\'s standard VAT is a fixed 7% of the taxable base, and subtotal + vat (after any discount) must equal the total.\n\nOutput ONE JSON object, no markdown, no explanation:\n{"subtotal": "number-as-string or null", "vat": "number-as-string or null", "discount": "number-as-string or null (omit or empty string if none printed)", "total_amount": "number-as-string or null"}\nNo currency symbols, no thousand separators.'


# ── ADR-013 读票流程（2026-09-27，与 ERP `recognition.policy` 同一套先后与措辞）────────────────────────
# 直读没过金额 / 合理性检查时，先用同一模型带提示复核一次；仍不过，再把 Vision 原文和原图一起给同一模型读。
#
# 看图读用下面这份精简提示词（用户 2026-09-27：「把 cowork 调到和 erp 同样的效果和速度及成本」）：L2_SYSTEM 约 1.2 万字符，
# 每次读图都要付这份输入，还要求模型为每个金额 / 税号 / 日期写 source_refs（来源栏位），输出多出一倍；来源栏位只用于
# 表格 / Excel 的「金额取自描述栏」检查，图片没有栏位。这里保留影响对错的规则、同一套输出字段，空字段可不写。
# 表格与 PDF 文字层仍走 L2_SYSTEM，不受影响。

IMAGE_SYSTEM = """You are an accountant reading the attached image of a Thai purchase document. Read every character from the image and output ONE JSON object (no markdown, no explanation). Always output invoice_number, date, subtotal, vat and total_amount (vat "0" only when the document prints no VAT); other fields may be omitted when not printed.

{"document_type": "tax_invoice"|"simplified_tax_invoice"|"receipt"|"credit_note"|"payment_evidence"|"order_evidence"|"other",
 "is_not_invoice": false, "is_copy_or_duplicate": false,
 "invoice_number": "", "date": "YYYY-MM-DD Gregorian", "date_raw": "date exactly as printed",
 "seller_name": "", "seller_tax": "13 digits", "seller_branch": "", "seller_addr": "",
 "buyer_name": "", "buyer_tax": "13 digits", "buyer_branch": "", "buyer_addr": "",
 "subtotal": "pre-VAT base", "vat": "", "discount": "", "total_amount": "final net payable",
 "wht_rate": "", "wht_amount": "", "cash_amount": "", "change_amount": "",
 "payment_method": "cash|transfer|qr|card", "currency": "only if clearly not baht",
 "items": [{"name": "", "qty": "", "price": "", "subtotal": ""}],
 "notes": "", "category": "3-5 char summary in the items' language", "additional_invoices": []}

Rules:
1. Numbers: plain strings, no commas or currency symbols ("12450.00"). Tax IDs: exactly 13 digits, no dashes.
2. Dates: a Buddhist year (>= 2400) minus 543 gives the Gregorian year (2569 -> 2026). Always copy date_raw as printed.
3. Names and addresses exactly as printed; never correct or translate them. Seller = the issuer at the top; buyer = the customer (ลูกค้า / ผู้ซื้อ / Customer / Sold to) with its own tax ID.
4. Items: every line item with a product/service name, in order; stitch a POS item wrapped over 2-3 lines into one. Skip subtotal / VAT / total / cash / change / discount / reprint-marker rows. Keep repeated lines. A line starting with "-" is an option of the item above: keep it only if it has its own price, without the "-".
5. total_amount is the final net payable (Total / NET / ยอดสุทธิ / รวมสุทธิ / ยอดชำระ), after discounts; never the cash tendered (cash_amount) or change (change_amount). discount = total discount as printed. On a 7-Eleven / POS slip printing "ยอดรวม 115 / ส่วนลด 5 / ยอดสุทธิ 110 / เงินสด 200 / เงินทอน 90", total_amount = 110 (not 115, not 200).
6. subtotal is the pre-VAT base: when VAT is included in the total, subtotal = total - VAT. Copy a printed VAT exactly; never recompute it (VAT-exempt items make it smaller than 7/107 of the total).
7. Credit note (ใบลดหนี้ — money direction, critical): document_type "credit_note" and copy amount signs exactly as printed: a printed "-2,809.82" or "(2,809.82)" MUST become "-2809.82" in subtotal, vat, total_amount and the items. Never turn a printed negative into a positive number: a credit note recorded as positive reverses the money direction.
8. Fuel receipts: liters in qty, price per liter in price; loyalty points are never money or quantity. Never invent a total you cannot read.
9. WHT (หัก ณ ที่จ่าย), payment_method, currency: only when printed; never guess.
10. document_type: "tax_invoice" = full ใบกำกับภาษี with a legal เลขที่ and the seller's 13-digit tax ID (fuel receipts included when they have both). "simplified_tax_invoice" = ใบกำกับภาษีอย่างย่อ / ABB / shop POS slip: keep the receipt running number as printed; on "R#0000970791P2 :0302013" the invoice number is the R# part, the ":0302013" is the store code. "payment_evidence" = bank transfer / PromptPay slip. "order_evidence" = online-shop order screenshot (order no. as invoice_number). Otherwise "receipt".
11. is_not_invoice = true only for a letter, contract, blank page, purchase order, quotation, a bare delivery note (no ใบกำกับภาษี in the title) or a bare card-approval slip with no goods and no seller tax ID. "ใบส่งของ/ใบกำกับภาษี" is a tax invoice. is_copy_or_duplicate = true when marked สำเนา / COPY / DUPLICATE.
12. Several invoices on one image (more than one invoice number / header / grand total): the first goes in the top-level fields, each other one as a complete object in additional_invoices. Never merge or drop one.
13. Branch (สาขา): seller_branch / buyer_branch = that party's branch as printed next to its name or tax ID, as 5 digits: "สำนักงานใหญ่" / "Head Office" / "HQ" -> "00000"; "สาขาที่ 18" / "สาขา 00018" / "Branch 18" -> "00018". Empty when not printed. Never copy one party's branch to the other.
14. invoice_number is the number the issuer printed (เลขที่ / No.), never one stamped or handwritten later by the buyer (accounting voucher stamps such as RR690609-001, PV / JV numbers)."""


def build_recheck_prompt(previous, reason):
    """带提示复核：给出第一次的读数和没过的检查，请模型看原图改读错的、保留读对的。"""
    keep = previous.model_dump(mode='json', exclude_none=True, exclude_defaults=True, exclude={'source_refs'})
    return (IMAGE_SYSTEM + '\n\nA first reading of this document returned:\n'
            + json.dumps(keep, ensure_ascii=False) + f'\nIt failed these checks: {reason}.\n'
            'Look at the document again carefully, especially the parts these checks concern (amounts at the foot, '
            'line amounts, discounts, tax IDs, dates), correct what was misread and return the complete JSON in the '
            'same format. Keep values that were read correctly.')


OCR_TRANSCRIPT_NOTE = ('\n\nAn OCR transcript of this image follows. Use the image for the layout and the transcript to '
                       'read every digit exactly.\n\n')
